{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwaZMuNPBngeXZpKCwYxXs","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (52.4KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/436debb7-5218-4b93-aebc-5d8d93edb760/tool-results/b2cg54lgr.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection (\"Shell Company\": `?path=/app/static%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`), D17 password\nreset token not bound to its account (\"Reset Expectations\": own token + victim `account_id`), D18 GraphQL resolver\nwithout field-level authz (\"Resolver Revolt\": `case(id:\"<protected_reference>\"){note}`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + zero or one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`).\nD11-D13 and D15 had NO concept key: the prompt and the bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and\nechoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never `effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says\n`worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class.\nMastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets since D15), described only by today's prompt.\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"436debb7-5218-4b93-aebc-5d8d93edb760","uuid":"1f165bb3-085a-4cec-8696-04d56cec13bd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:05:03.319Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection (\"Shell Company\": `?path=/app/static%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`), D17 password\nreset token not bound to its account (\"Reset Expectations\": own token + victim `account_id`), D18 GraphQL resolver\nwithout field-level authz (\"Resolver Revolt\": `case(id:\"<protected_reference>\"){note}`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + zero or one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`).\nD11-D13 and D15 had NO concept key: the prompt and the bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and\nechoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never `effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says\n`worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class.\nMastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets since D15), described only by today's prompt.\nPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\ncal. 25 -> D19-D31 (13 lane-days) over cal. 26-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in D19-D27.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\nupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\nOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL (same `protected_reference`/case/note shape as\nD14 behind a resolver). Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18). D18's prompt (\"vary the\nprotocol surface without changing the underlying authorization discipline\") and D17's multi-step flow point at:\nmore auth-flow bugs (JWT/session forgery, MFA/OTP step skip, OAuth redirect_uri), other API surfaces (WebSocket,\nbatched/aliased GraphQL, version-swapped REST), and the untouched classics (XXE, DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype\npollution, NoSQL, deserialization, race, CORS, header trust, CRLF, cache poisoning).\nSnapshot 2026-10-25 (after D18). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS): D23 SSTI,\nsecond-order, mass assignment; D24 field/action authz, SSRF; D25 `day25_web_shell_company` (KEY\n`example_path|input_parameter|command|shell|exec`), `day25_web_reset_expectations` (KEY `reco