{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DfJFsWF4FD9XZbHw22znea","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t# Web coverage atlas\n     2\t\n     3\tLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\n     4\tquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\n     5\tclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\n     6\tunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\n     7\tsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\n     8\tD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\n     9\tD16 OS command injection (\"Shell Company\": `?path=/app/static%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`), D17 password\n    10\treset token not bound to its account (\"Reset Expectations\": own token + victim `account_id`), D18 GraphQL resolver\n    11\twithout field-level authz (\"Resolver Revolt\": `case(id:\"<protected_reference>\"){note}`). Since D05 every target is\n    12\tthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n    13\t`current_user`) + zero or one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n    14\t`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n    15\t`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`).\n    16\tD11-D13 and D15 had NO concept key: the prompt and the bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and\n    17\techoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never `effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says\n    18\t`worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class.\n    19\tMastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets since D15), described only by today's prompt.\n    20\tPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\n    21\tcal. 25 -> D19-D31 (13 lane-days) over cal. 26-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in D19-D27.\n    22\tArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\n    23\tupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\n    24\tOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL (same `protected_reference`/case/note shape as\n    25\tD14 behind a resolver). Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18). D18's prompt (\"vary the\n    26\tprotocol surface without changing the underlying authorization discipline\") and D17's multi-step flow point at:\n    27\tmore auth-flow bugs (JWT/session forgery, MFA/OTP step skip, OAuth redirect_uri), other API surfaces (WebSocket,\n    28\tbatched/aliased GraphQL, version-swapped REST), and the untouched classics (XXE, DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype\n    29\tpollution, NoSQL, deserialization, race, CORS, header trust, CRLF, cache poisoning).\n    30\tSnapshot 2026-10-25 (after D18). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n    31\t`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS): D23 SSTI,\n    32\tsecond-order, mass assignment; D24 field/action authz, SSRF; D25 `day25_web_shell_company` (KEY\n    33\t`example_path|input_parameter|command|shell|exec`), `day25_web_reset_expectations` (KEY `recovery_guide_route|..`),\n    34\t`day25_web_resolver_revolt` (KEY `protected_reference|resolver|graphql|..`, overlaps D14's key -> both race).\n    35\t`hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys exist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap is pending.\n    36\t\n    37\tStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`, handler in\n    38\t`lib/web/handlers/`). `gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies\n    39\tin -> request plan `[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver fetches.\n    40\t\n    41\t## Coverage table\n    42\t\n    43\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n    44\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    45\t| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x3) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n    46\t| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (Mastery x2) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n    47\t| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family + quote-balanced | done; Mastery |\n    48\t| 3b | second-order SQLi (stored value queried later) | seen D12 | \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":..}` | POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET secondary; `rows[]` holds proof | done; Mastery |\n    49\t| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (Mastery) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n    50\t| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n    51\t| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie, `X-Role` in errors | flip the value the app names | high (D13 did the body form) |\n    52\t| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high |\n    53\t| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n    54\t| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | seen D13 | \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary 403 `administrator_required` | POST JSON `display_name` + role/is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions, GET secondary | done; Mastery |\n    55\t| 10 | OS command injection | seen D16 | \"a little too close to a real shell\", \"give it something to do\", clues `input_parameter` + `example_path`, 400 `path_required`, JSON `stdout` | `?<param>=<example>%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (raw `;` dropped by Go) | done; Mastery |\n    56\t| 11 | SSTI (expression in a rendered message) | seen D11 | \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` | `?template={{7*7}}` -> 49, then `{{objective}}` | done; Mastery |\n    57\t| 11b | SSTI sequels: sandbox escape / file read / stored template | gap | `{{objective}}` absent or filtered, \"sandbox\", \"safe mode\", stored profile rendered later | engine fingerprint -> per-engine file read of prompt path | med |\n    58\t| 12 | SSRF to an internal-only route | seen D15 (Mastery x4 targets) | \"will fetch anything you point it at\", \"places you can't reach yourself\", \"internal service\", feature 400 `absolute_url_required`, secondary 403 `internal_only` | `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` (port 80 = `fetch_failed`) | done; Mastery |\n    59\t| 12b | 