{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019KsPccVihVnTw2MMgWj7Vr","type":"tool_result","content":"60:- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n61-  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed\n62-  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17). Re-dealt within a day: D12 result ->\n63-  internal, D13 audit -> internal, D15 account -> internal, D16 process -> execute, D17 result -> audit, D18 inspect\n64-  -> submit. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or the guide JSON's `*_route` keys), never by the word in the value.\n65-- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D18) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only feature (D05,\n66-  D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user` and dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key -> classify from\n67-  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,\n68-  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers.\n69-- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n70-  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin (D16), Symfony (D17), GraphQL.js (D18, title only). Rule: ignore it -- except\n71-  that a Go server drops a raw `;` from the query string (percent-encode).\n72-- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds. Rule: JSON first.\n73-- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`\n74-  (depth-2 crawl). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))`\n75-  `\"` + `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + prompt path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07\n76-  board noun `messages` | `postcards` from openapi. D09 outside mailbox option `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`,\n77-  token sent or not. D10 preview URL from the upload response's `path`, syntax from the guide's `<code>`.\n78-- **SSTI (D11)**: param `template` (others rendered empty); `{{..}}` evaluated, `${..}`/`*{..}` literal under a\n79-  \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var `objective`. Rule: one probe per param holding every delimiter family with\n80-  distinct arithmetic, keep the family that evaluated, then ask for `objective`.\n81-- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single), `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT) as JSON in every common field;\n82-  re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant. **Mass assignment (D13)**: one JSON body `display_name` + `role`,\n83-  `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles`, `access_level`, `permissions`; echo hides which bound.\n84-- **API field/action authz (D14)**: inventory `fields` `[title, note]`, `actions` `[view, export]`; single pair\n85-  (`note`+`export`) skips the check; lists and `*` forbidden. Rule: every SINGLE field x action from the inventory.\n86-- **SSRF (D15)**: `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` in single, TT, Mastery; port 80/5000/8000/3000 =\n87-  `fetch_failed`. Rule: host ladder, port ladder, param from the error word, else `url`.\n88-- **Command injection (D16)**: `input_parameter: path` and `example_path: /app/static` constant across single, TT,\n89-  Mastery; base command `ls -ld <path>` (stdout echoed). Rule: param from `input_parameter` (else the `<x>_required`\n90-  error), value = example + `%3B` + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (then `\\n`, `&&`, `|`, `$()`).\n91-- **Password reset (D17)**: guide JSON `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter: account_id,\n92-  token_parameter: token, accounts:[{id,label,self_service}]}` same keys in single/TT; ids, token (12 hex) and route\n93-  words differ. Rule: request a token for the `self_service:true` id, redeem it with each `self_service:false` id.\n94-- **GraphQL resolver (D18)**: schema identical in single/TT/Mastery (`caseIndex:[CaseReference{id,title,\n95-  visibility}]`, `case(id:ID!):Case{id,title,note}`); `protected_reference` is a STRING id. Rule: introspect, then\n96-  call every arg-taking Query field with the protected id selecting all scalars; POST JSON first, then GET\n97-  `?query=`, then form (\"vary the protocol surface\" -- POST JSON was enough every time).\n98-- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL\n99-  `data.<alias>.note`, a receipt on a board page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on\n100-  field names or on `effect`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"436debb7-5218-4b93-aebc-5d8d93edb760","uuid":"f6cbe61f-d6d4-42b9-8c7c-9cbfd08950df","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:07:47.487Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"60:- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n61-  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed\n62-  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17). Re-dealt within a day: D12 result ->\n63-  internal, D13 audit -> internal, D15 account -> internal, D16 process -> execute, D17 result -> audit, D18 inspect\n64-  -> submit. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or the guide JSON's `*_route` keys), never by the word in the value.\n65-- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D18) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only feature (D05,\n66-  D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user` and dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key -> classify from\n67-  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,\n68-  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers.\n69-- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Larav