{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJEaeT54LC4nKyce7S2QMw","type":"tool_result","content":"203:## Pitfalls that cost time\n204-- Shipping a new day without its class handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15, D16, D17, D18,\n205-  and D16 Mastery missed today's target. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single\n206-  submit, like D11 did; the single solves now take ~40 s, so the plugin is the long pole.\n207-- Treating `effect` as success: D12 prints its effect with `rows: []`; D16 prints `worker_command_completed` for\n208-  the plain `ls`. Success = proof regex.\n209-- Raw `;` in a Go (Gin) query string is dropped -> the param looks missing. Always `--data-urlencode` / `%3B`.\n210-- GraphQL routes 404 on GET; POST JSON `{\"query\":...}` before writing the route off.\n211-- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n212-- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n213-- SSRF to the default port: D15's internal service listens on 8080; `fetch_failed` = wrong port, not \"blocked\".\n214-- Combining fields (`title,note`, `*`) in D14 was forbidden; only the single bypassed pair works.\n215-- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\".\n216-- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (re-dealt every attempt) or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level\n217-  crawls (D01). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.\n218-- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n219-- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n220-- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\", \"self-service only\" on REQUEST but not REDEEM).\n221-- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n222-\n223-## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n224-- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n225-  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n226-  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n227-- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n228-- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n228 reference/techniques/web.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"436debb7-5218-4b93-aebc-5d8d93edb760","uuid":"e647e2c6-10b1-40c7-909a-72fd11622a5b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:08:27.597Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"203:## Pitfalls that cost time\n204-- Shipping a new day without its class handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15, D16, D17, D18,\n205-  and D16 Mastery missed today's target. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single\n206-  submit, like D11 did; the single solves now take ~40 s, so the plugin is the long pole.\n207-- Treating `effect` as success: D12 prints its effect with `rows: []`; D16 prints `worker_command_completed` for\n208-  the plain `ls`. Success = proof regex.\n209-- Raw `;` in a Go (Gin) query string is dropped -> the param looks missing. Always `--data-urlencode` / `%3B`.\n210-- GraphQL routes 404 on GET; POST JSON `{\"query\":...}` before writing the route off.\n211-- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n212-- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n213-- SSRF to the default port: D15's internal service listens on 8080; `fetch_failed` = wrong port, not \"blocked\".\n214-- Combining fields (`title,note`, `*`) in D14 was forbidden; only the single bypassed pair works.\n215-- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\".\n216-- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (re-dealt every attempt) or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level\n217-  crawls (D01). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.\n218-- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n219-- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n220-- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\", \"self-service only\" on REQUEST but not REDEEM).\n221-- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n222-\n223-## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n224-- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n225-  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n226-  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n227-- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n228-- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n228 reference/techniques/web.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GJEaeT54LC4nKyce7S2QMw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
