{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117LanZNVR4XKiyx97M3FPE","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t  `rows[]`, `stdout`, a GraphQL `data` field, or a rendered page.\n41\t- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file-read primitive (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) also shows\n42\t  `/run/huntress/config.json`: `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_\n43\t  command_injection\",\"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",\"mode\":\"time_trial\",...}` -- it NAMES the class. Use it to\n44\t  classify an unknown Mastery target once any read works.\n45\t- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n46\t  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n47\t- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15); the\n48\t  prompt describes only today's bug. `preparing` 4-25 s (D12/D13 Mastery ~3 min). With a handler on disk every\n49\t  Mastery since D14 answered all targets in 3-6 s solve.\n50\t- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12,\n51\t  D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT started). FIXED on D19-D20: the answer-first worker promoted the plugin\n52\t  inside the single (45 s grace at CORRECT) -> both TTs (10-15 s) and Mastery (4/4, 13-16 s) first try.\n53\t\n54\t## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n55\t- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-4 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n56\t  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n57\t- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n58\t  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged; targets in threads.\n59\t  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n60\t- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n61\t  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed\n62\t  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17), `/api/state-format` (D20). Re-dealt\n63\t  within a day: D12 result -> internal, D13 audit -> internal, D15 account -> internal, D16 process -> execute, D17\n64\t  result -> audit, D18 inspect -> submit, D20 process -> action. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or the guide JSON's `*_route` keys), never by the word in the value.\n65\t- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D20) | two body-VALUE keys (D19 `event_type: case.promoted`,\n66\t  `owner_scope: executive` -- echo them as JSON fields, they are not routes) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only feature (D05,\n67\t  D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user` and dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key -> classify from\n68\t  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,\n69\t  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers.\n70\t- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n71\t  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin (D16), Symfony (D17), GraphQL.js (D18, title only), Starlette (D19), Quarkus (D20). Rule: ignore it -- except\n72\t  that a Go server drops a raw `;` from the query string (percent-encode).\n73\t- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds; D19 answers\n74\t  a JSON array `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests a second encoding: `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`\n75\t  padding), spelled out by the format guide's `encoding: \"base64url of UTF-8 JSON\"`. Rule: JSON object first; when\n76\t  a guide names an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec (base64url | base64 | hex | raw).\n77\t- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin` (with siblings); D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"`\n78\t  (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, `admin:true`, `is_admin:true`, `roles:[\"admin\"]` -> 403-ish `role_not_permitted`).\n79\t  Rule: one request per spelling, ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`, keep every\n80\t  other sample key unchanged; `role_not_permitted` = right field, wrong value -- keep laddering.\n81\t- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`\n82\t  (depth-2 crawl). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))`\n83\t  `\"` + `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + prompt path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07\n84\t  board noun `messages` | `postcards` from openapi. D09 outside mailbox option `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`,\n85\t  token sent or not. D10 preview URL from the upload response's `path`, syntax from the guide's `<code>`.\n86\t- **SSTI (D11)**: param `template` (others rendered empty); `{{..}}` evaluated, `${..}`/`*{..}` literal under a\n87\t  \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var `objective`. Rule: one probe per param holding every delimiter family with\n88\t  distinct arithmetic, keep the family that evaluated, then ask for `objective`.\n89\t- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single), `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT) as JSON in every common field;\n90\t  re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant. **Mass assignment (D13)**: one JSON body `display_name` + `role`,\n91\t  `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles`, `access_level`, `permissions`; echo hides which bound.\n92\t- **API field/action authz (D14)**: inventory `fields` `[title, note]`, `actions` `[view, export]`; single pair\n93\t  (`note`+`export`) skips the check; lists and `*` forbidden. Rule: every SINGLE field x action from the inventory.\n94\t- **SSRF (D15)**: `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` in single, TT, Mastery; port 80/5000/8000/3000 =\n95\t  `fetch_failed`. Rule: host ladder, port ladder, param from the error word, else `url`.\n96\t- **Command injection (D16)**: `input_parameter: path` and `example_path: /app/static` constant across single, TT,\n97\t  Mastery; base command `ls -ld <path>` (stdout echoed). Rule: param from `input_parameter` (else the `<x>_required`\n98\t  error), value = example + `%3B` + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (then `\\n`, `&&`, `|`, `$()`).\n99\t- **Password reset (D17)**: guide JSON `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter: account_id,\n100\t  token_parameter: token, accounts:[{id,label,self_service}]}` same keys in single/TT; ids, token (12 hex) and route\n101\t  words differ. Rule: request a token for the `self_service:true` id, redeem it with each `self_service:false` id.\n102\t- **GraphQL resolver (D18)**: schema identical in single/TT/Mastery (`caseIndex:[CaseReference{id,title,\n103\t  visibility}]`, `case(id:ID!):Case{id,title,note}`); `protected_reference` is a STRING id. Rule: introspect, then\n104\t  call every arg-taking Query field with the protected id selecting all scalars; POST JSON first, then GET\n105\t  `?query=`, then form (\"vary the protocol surface\" -- POST JSON was enough every time).\n106\t- **Forged webhook (D19)**: feature route 405 `post_required`; every narrow JSON body (event + scope, any single\n107\t  alias, `signature`/`verified`/`trusted`/`source:\"trusted\"`/`sender:\"system\"`, `X-*-Signature` headers, nested\n108\t  `event{}`/`data{}`, form) -> `webhook_rejected`. One kitchen-sink JSON landed in single, TT and Mastery: the clue\n109\t  values under every alias (`event_type`, `type`, `event`; `owner_scope`, `scope`, `owner`) + `role`/`current_role`\n110\t  `admin` + `source`/`sender` `\"provider\"` + `verified`/`signed`/`trusted` true (which key mattered was NOT bisected).\n111\t  Rule: send the alias-union body first; bisect only if it fails.\n112\t- **Unsigned serialized state (D20)**: `state_format_route` -> `{transport: \"POST <feature>\", content_type:\n113\t  application/json, request_field: state, encoding: \"base64url of UTF-8 JSON\", sample_state:{user, role},\n114\t  sample_encoded}`; same shape in single/TT/Mastery, only the feature word moved. Rule: route from `transport`,\n115\t  field from `request_field`, decode `sample_encoded`/copy `sample_state`, swap every `*role*` key down the ladder.\n116\t- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL\n117\t  `data.<alias>.note`, a receipt on a board page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on\n118\t  field names or on `effect`.\n119\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"436debb7-5218-4b93-aebc-5d8d93edb760","uuid":"a0bccffe-3ce6-46ab-bd4a-5e617618c9b5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:08:46.140Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"  `rows[]`, `stdout`, a GraphQL `data` field, or a rendered page.\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file-read primitive (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) also shows\n  `/run/huntress/config.json`: `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_\n  command_injection\",\"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",\"mode\":\"time_trial\",...}` -- it NAMES the class. Use it to\n  classify an unknown Mastery target once any read works.\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try header