{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQuHPGPV889n4Y7RBsUu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QYkT8qZJgZkq4PybPFXzf6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='reference/coverage/web.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:70]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\na=s.index('Lane: a LIVE'); b=s.index('Status legend:')\ns=s[:a]+'''Lane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection, D17 password reset token not bound to its account, D18 GraphQL resolver without\nfield-level authz, D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events (\"Trust the Webhook\": one JSON body with the\nclue `event_type`/`owner_scope` values under every alias + role/source/trust flags), D20 unsigned client-side state\nblob (\"Serialized Offender\": `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":..,\"role\":\"administrator\"}')}`). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + usually one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`,\n`event_type`+`owner_scope` (body values), `state_format_route`). D11-D13 and D15 had NO concept key: the prompt and\nthe bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and echoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never\n`effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says `worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows\n`/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class. Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets\nsince D15), described only by today's prompt.\nPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\ncal. 25, D19-D20 cal. 26 -> D21-D31 (11 lane-days) over cal. 27-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in\nD21-D28.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\nupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\nOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL -> integrity failures (OWASP A08 / API10: D19\nunsigned webhook, D20 unsigned state). Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18) and D19+D20\ncame as a pair; \"sign nothing\" points straight at the signed-but-weak sequel: JWT (`alg:none`, leaked/weak HS256\nsecret, kid/jku), signed cookies with a leaked secret, HMAC webhooks with a leaked secret or replayable timestamp,\nnative serialization (pickle/PHP/Java) gadgets. Still untouched OWASP Top-10 areas: A02 crypto failures\n(predictable/weak tokens), A05 misconfig (XXE, CORS, debug, default creds), A06 known-vulnerable component, A04\ninsecure design (race/business logic), A09 log injection; plus DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype pollution, NoSQL,\nWebSocket, CRLF, cache poisoning.\nSnapshot 2026-10-26 (after D20). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`,