{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQuNwBR2PbbNKzjewsJg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01744dT6v4WcNGqZwbXMw76T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/web.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index('Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days'); b=s.index('```json')\ns=s[:a]+'''Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D21-D28 at ~2-3 lane-days per day). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in; no\n`web:*` keys in .run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. After D15:\n`ssrf-planner`. After D18: `cmd-injection-planner`, `graphql-introspection`. After D20: `api-unsafe-consumption`\n(seen D19 -> `webhook-signature-sequels`); `deserialization-gadgets` narrowed to native/signed formats (unsigned JSON\nstate seen D20); `codify-before-tt` lowered to 2 (fixed on D19-D20). Added after D20: `webhook-signature-sequels`,\n`alias-union-body-builder`, `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `known-vulnerable-component`, `log-injection-forging`;\nraised: `jwt-session-forge` (first), `role-tamper-planner` detail (role ladder).\n\n'''+s[b:]\na=s.index('```json\\n')+len('```json\\n'); b=s.index('\\n```',a)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a:b])\nby={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['id']!='api-unsafe-consumption']\nby['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['detail']=(\"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). After D20 lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ still holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> nothing below has drained. Owner of the nightly batch: set HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or add web to the default AUTO_LANES) so the prebuild gaps below get built; fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\")\nby['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['concept']=\"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\"\ncb=by['codify-before-tt']; cb['priority']=2\ncb['detail']=(\"FIXED on D19-D20 (cal. 26): the answer-first worker promoted the plugin during the single (45 s grace at CORRECT, commit 4715290f) -> both Time Trials (10.2 s, 15.1 s) and both Mastery runs (4/4, 13-16 s) first try, the first new-class TTs to pass since D14. Before that TT went solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18 (plugins landed 0-2 s after TT start; D16 Mastery 3/4 with the plugin still `.tmp`). Keep: if a single needs >~90 s, gate TT start on the promoted plugin being importable.\")\nby['jwt-session-forge']['detail']=(\"D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing at a readable file), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json / *.pem route), jku/x5u to an app-owned route. Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1); Express `s:<val>.<sig>` (HMAC-SHA256 base64 no padding); generic `<b64 JSON>.<hex hmac>` blobs. Escalate with the D20 role ladder (administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner) on every `*role*`/`is_admin` claim, keep other claims. Reuse D20's format-guide reading (transport, request_field, encoding). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\")\nby['deserialization-gadgets']['concept']=\"native / signed serialization sequels: pickle, PHP, Java, node-serialize, .NET (row 21b)\"\nby['deserialization-gadgets']['detail']=(\"D20 saw the data-tamper form (unsigned base64url JSON `state` described by a format guide; role -> administrator). Sequel planner: recognise base64 blobs gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP serialize, length-prefixed strings -> fix s:N when editing), rO0 (Java), AAEAAAD (.NET BinaryFormatter), `_$$ND_FUNC$$_` (node-serialize), YAML `!!python`; first rewrite data fields (role/isAdmin/user) keeping the format's own length/type markers, then a minimal gadget that only reads /run/huntress/objective.txt (pickle __reduce__ -> open().read() returned into a field the app echoes). Encodings per guide (base64url/base64/hex/raw). Parser: proof regex / evidence.\")\nby['role-tamper-planner']['detail']=(\"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. D13 granted admin via JSON body binding, D20 via a role field inside an unsigned state blob -- and D20 accepted ONLY `administrator` (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, flags -> role_not_permitted). Remaining forms: cookie role=<value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role= / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route. Value ladder, one request each: administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager, plus any higher value the app lists; `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"webhook-signature-sequels\",\"concept\":\"webhook sequels: HMAC-signed events with a leaked/weak secret, replay, provider allowlist (row 44b)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D19 'Trust the Webh