{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQuSwCkrmYKqtH7y6Du4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both web files for day26 (lane-days D19 and D20). Both challenges went CORRECT first try in all three modes. I didn't run tests or touch any GM mode.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/web.md`** (now 211 lines):\n   - **D19 \"Trust the Webhook\"**: a webhook that accepts forged, unsigned events. Every narrow POST got `webhook_rejected`. One JSON body that put the clue values under every alias, plus admin role, `provider` source and trust flags, got the proof. Which field actually mattered was never tested.\n   - **D20 \"Serialized Offender\"**: an unsigned base64url JSON `state` blob described by `/api/state-format`. Only `role: \"administrator\"` worked; `admin` came back `role_not_permitted`.\n   - Each entry has the commands, new error/effect spellings and timings. Single solves took about 95 s and 100 s, Time Trials 10–15 s, Mastery 4/4 in 13–16 s.\n   - The plugins shipped before Time Trial this time, so the long-running \"Time Trial fails on a new class\" problem is marked fixed.\n   - New variant axes: base64url state encoding, which spelling of \"admin\" a target accepts, the webhook body shape, the `process` → `action` route-word swap, and two new framework banners. New pitfalls: about 60 s lost testing one field at a time against a rejection that names no field, and giving up on role values after `admin`.\n   - To stay near 200 lines, I compressed the D01–D18 day entries and the older variant axes.\n2. **`reference/coverage/web.md`**:\n   - Marked unsigned serialized state \"seen D20\" and forged webhooks \"seen D19\". Added rows for the signed follow-ups (native deserialization, signed webhooks) and three untouched OWASP areas: weak/derivable tokens, known-vulnerable components, log injection.\n   - Recognition cues gained D19/D20 lines and are exactly at the 60-line cap.\n   - In the readiness gaps, I dropped the webhook gap (now seen) and moved JWT forging to the top. \"Sign nothing\" points at weak-key signing (JWT, signed cookies, HMAC webhooks) next. I added `webhook-signature-sequels` and `alias-union-body-builder` at priority 1, and lowered `codify-before-tt` to 2. The JSON is valid, with 46 gaps, 40 of them unbuilt prebuilds.\n   - The web prebuild lane now exists in `hctf/prebuild.py`, but it only runs with `HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1`. Nothing has been built yet, so none of these gaps will be worked on overnight until that flag is set."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1088,"cache_read_input_tokens":132858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1088},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"436debb7-5218-4b93-aebc-5d8d93edb760","uuid":"7d1b9668-706d-43e4-b434-b93dbe082fd0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:11:31.540Z","request_id":"req_011CgQuSvtuDoLp8QpGU1SAJ"}
